# Multi-Zone PIR Home Security System

## Description
An advanced home security system using multiple PIR motion sensors placed in 
different zones/rooms. Each zone has its own dedicated buzzer, allowing 
independent motion detection and alerting across multiple areas simultaneously.

## Components Used
- Arduino Uno R3
- 4x PIR Motion Sensors
- 4x Buzzers

## Circuit Connections
| Component | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| PIR Sensor 1 (OUT) | Digital Pin 2 |
| PIR Sensor 2 (OUT) | Digital Pin 3 |
| PIR Sensor 3 (OUT) | Digital Pin 4 |
| PIR Sensor 4 (OUT) | Digital Pin 5 |
| Buzzer 1 (+) | Digital Pin 8 |
| Buzzer 2 (+) | Digital Pin 9 |
| Buzzer 3 (+) | Digital Pin 10 |
| Buzzer 4 (+) | Digital Pin 11 |

## How It Works
1. Each PIR sensor independently monitors its assigned zone for motion.
2. When motion is detected in a zone, that zone's buzzer is triggered.
3. Each zone operates independently — multiple zones can be triggered at once.
4. Serial Monitor logs which zone detected motion, useful for tracking activity.

